            form: "Plain past + ら: 行ったら, 高かったら, 静かだったら, 雨だったら (negative: 行かなかったら)",
            note: "〜たら is the all-purpose conditional: once A happens (or if A is true), B. Unlike と and ば, it can be followed by requests, invitations and plans: 駅に着いたら電話してください. It also means \"when A is done\" for things that will surely happen (二十歳になったら), and with a past ending it means \"I did A and found B\": 家に帰ったら、荷物が届いていた. In that discovery use, B is something you notice, not something you chose to do. Compare なら, which takes the other person's topic or plan as given (行くなら, if you're going), and と, which is for automatic results.",
            examples: [("駅に着いたら、電話してください。", "Call me when you get to the station."), ("もし雨だったら、試合は中止です。", "If it rains, the game is off."), ("家に帰ったら、母が来ていた。", "When I got home, I found my mom had come over.")],
            keywords: ["たら", "conditional", "if", "when"],
