            note: "とき means \"at the time when\". With verbs, the tense inside the とき clause shows order, not the time of the whole sentence: 日本に行くとき、かばんを買った means you bought it before or on the way (the going wasn't finished yet), while 日本に行ったとき、かばんを買った means you bought it in Japan, after arriving. So 寝るとき is \"when going to bed\" and 寝たとき is \"after falling asleep\". Don't forget な and の: 暇なとき, 子どものとき. Compare 〜たら, which is a condition, and 〜前に／〜後で, which only give the order.",
